{
  "model": "models/HumanDecision.tla",
  "scope": "HJ0 finite behavioral models only; two cards/two competing replies, three calls/two sessions, three inputs/two sessions. Includes weak-fairness conditional progress. No runtime, SQL, power-loss, real scheduling fairness or distributed protocol proof. RecoveryRouting: one runtime replacement, durable answer/inbox and generation-fenced receiver with weak-fairness conditional delivery. AuthorityComposition: seven independent withdrawal sources and one protected commit; abstract atomic owner guards, not an implemented coordinator. RegistrationProtocol: one original operation and bounded duplicate IDs, durable registration/seal and volatile receipts. ContinuationComposition: two rounds with two cards, one runtime replacement, current authority/terminal fencing and recorded judgments; abstract atomic recording, no arbitrary external effect proof. IntakeControl: one session, three inputs, pending capacity two, two driver generations and archive/run cancellation; logical scheduling only. ExecutionSlots: three calls, one active slot, one human wait; human release, ready queue, reacquire and conditional progress under weak fairness. Continuation includes mixed allow/ask/deny judgments in the second round and ready-to-advance conditional progress. GovernanceAdoption: two leases and two adopters, complete candidates, revision/evidence guards and atomic bundle publication; trusted evidence is an abstract premise.",
